    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "The substantive prayer made in the petition reads thus:\n't is, therefore, respectfully prayed that the present petition may kindly be allowed and the above said FIR No. 0407 dated 07.10.2021 (Annexure P- 1) registered under Sections 406, 467, 468, 420, 471 IPC at Police Station- Israna,\nDistt-Panipat may kindly be quashed qua the petitioner, on the basis of Compromise held between the parties in pursuance of their compromise dated 06.06.2025 (Annexure P-2), in the interest of justice.\nFurther Prayed that the further proceedings arising out of the above- mentioned FIR (Annexure P-1)\nmay kindly be stayed qua the petitioner, in the interest of justice.\nFurther prayed that the petitioner may kindly be exempted from filing the certified/typed copies of the Annexures P-1 to P-5 and permit him to file the photocopies and true typed copies in the interest of justice.'\n2. Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner seeks to withdraw 1 of 2 the petition in hand with Jitender vs State Of Haryana And Others on 6 March, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/189709112/\n1 liberty to file afresh on the same cause of action after arraying all concerned in view of the dicta of Division Bench of this Court in CRM-M No.48043 of 2023 titled Rakesh Dass v. State of Haryana and another, decided on 22.11.2024.\n3.",
